<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Pyramids</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1798">1798</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Embabeh · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Pyramids was fought on 21 July 1798 at Embabeh on the west bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>, during the French campaign in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a>'s army, formed in infantry squares, repelled the charges of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> cavalry of Murad Bey and inflicted heavy losses at small cost. The victory opened Cairo to the French and broke Mamluk rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-egypt">Lower Egypt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-pyramids.jpg" alt="Battle of the Pyramids" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François-Louis-Joseph Watteau · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francois-Louis-Joseph_Watteau_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
